  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between 1-deoxymannojirimycin and Elongation factor 1-alpha 2, as it is indirectly linked through multiple target pathways. The drug 1-deoxymannojirimycin is observed to interact with several kinases, including Serine/threonine-protein kinase D2 and Cell division cycle 2-like protein kinase 6, which in turn target Dehydrobruceine B. Dehydrobruceine B is known to have a target of Elongation factor 1-alpha 2, and similarly, another pathway involving Cyclin-dependent kinase-like 3 also leads to the same target. These findings collectively indicate that 1-deoxymannojirimycin may exert its effects through a series of kinase-mediated interactions, ultimately influencing the activity of Elongation factor 1-alpha 2. The evidence is supported by multiple high-scoring pathways, suggesting a plausible biological mechanism. However, the exact nature of the interaction and its functional significance remain to be fully elucidated.",
